Z||000005||hugh||11-12-2000||09:57 AM||||I don't have any pictures to post.My Max was a Husky,we had to let him go last September.He had developed a huge tumor on one of his hips.He was about 11 years old,but until he got sick ,he was like a puppy.I loved him because he was so independant.I would go out on the back porch and ask him if he wanted to come in.If he did he would,if he didn't he would just ignore me.My neighbor(who doesn't even like dogs,probably because he is over 70 and doesn't have the patience)used to get dog bones for Max and give him a few every day.When Max would see him in his yard he would call him.If any of you are familiar with Huskies,they don't bark.If you grabbed Max around the neck he sounded like he was going to tear you apart if he got loose and that made people unsure of him,until they got to know him,then they loved him.He would holler at me if I smacked him on the butt to let me know he didn't like it.I really miss him.   ||||reg||1
